paragraph start
name: paragraph-tp-vision-purpose
The ecosystem does not only map information. Its main purpose is
to turn what is written into something lived: a routine, a testing
field, a learning path. Tracks are where this happens, so they are
a core feature of the whole system and not an add-on.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tp-vision-whole
Every decision here is made for the whole ecosystem: runfile,
editor, shell, server and web page. A track touches all of them,
so no module is planned alone.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tp-vision-changes
Expect changes outside this plan: the runfile formatting, the
marks, the block types, the index and the server commands. The web
page needs new features too: a live checklist, a walk view, level
and progress views. Each change is decided here before it is built.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tp-vision-method
Method: sets of about twenty questions with options, each set
labeled with how advanced it is. Answers are written into this page
at once. Building starts only when the plan is closed.
