paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-marks-syntax
Several marks in one declaration are separated by commas, for
example mark: rule, step, card. Why: one line, easy to read and to
edit. Example: a block marked rule and check carries both.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-mark-kinds
Mark kinds work like block types. The built-in kinds are files in
the default runfile folder. Users add their own kinds in the
nearest .runfile subfolder, which adds on top of the default one.
Why: a new kind needs no code and no copy of the defaults.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-layout-marks
Marking files and directories. A layout file may hold a mark block
and may mark the title of a file it links, which marks that file. A
file can also be marked inside itself. Why: a layout card is already
a link to the real file, so the mark follows the link.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end



paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-progress-scope
Progress belongs to the part it measures. A day holds several
chains, a chain holds several steps, and each one has its own
progress. Why: a day can be done while one chain is half done.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-ai
The AI may change anything in these files when he asks: steps,
levels, times, chains and marks. The branch history is the record
and the way back.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-modular
Everything is modular and combines freely. Repeat kinds, time
kinds, timer kinds, pauses and measures are parts that nest in any
order. Example: a repeat inside a timer, with a pause inside the
repeat. Planned repeats: N times, every N minutes until a time,
spaced repetition, forced recurrence. Planned timers: countdown,
countup, interval work and rest, wait until a clock time, and more
later. New kinds are added without changing the others.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-measure
A measure may hold a number, a unit, a target, a tolerance, a
history and a formula between measures. Why: reps, minutes, weight
and waits are all the same thing with a different unit.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-regress
Regress is modular. It can go back in time by a bigger or smaller
amount, back one level, or back more, and each step may define its
own rule. A rule has a trigger and an amount, both set by him.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-chains
Chain, include and parallel all exist and each is a part of its
own. Why: a day is a chain, a body routine is an include and the
hourly and daily tracks run in parallel. If the same step comes
twice in one chain it shows twice, and only a program removes it.
Why: a repeat is there for a reason.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d2-server
The editor, the runfile system and the web page all work through
the server and never alone. The web page has as much control as the
editor, with a defined interface, plus and minus controls instead
of typing. Its own plan comes after the fundamentals.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
