paragraph start
name: paragraph-d3-worktree
Track files live in a git worktree: a second folder of the same
repo with its own branch, so both trees are always on disk. The
index loads both folders and links work by name, not by path.
Reading two trees is cheap. Why not a plain branch: a checkout
would swap the files and the track files would vanish.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d3-server
The server is part of the ecosystem and first class. Everything
goes through it. There is no offline mode to plan for.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end


paragraph start
name: paragraph-d3-chain-end
A chain ends only when he stops it. The commit happens on that
stop. This also covers a year or a parallel chain, which never end
by themselves.
