paragraph start
name: paragraph-d6-progress
Progress is an append-only event log. Each step instance holds its
events in the progress file of its worktree, and its state is
computed from them: running, done, skipped, level, due. State is
never stored as the truth. Why: nothing is lost, a new scheduling
kind can be added later and read the old events, and regress is
just another event. An optional snapshot may be added later for
speed.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d6-events
An instance records everything: start, done, skip, snooze, jump,
pause, resume, regress with its rule, level change, measure values,
timer events, note links and who made the change. The event kinds
are open, a new kind needs no change to the others.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d6-schedule
Scheduling kinds are blocks that read the events: fixed clock,
relative, sun, month, year, decade, and later spaced repetition
such as SM-2 or FSRS. Spaced repetition runs per step instance.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-d6-marks
Built-in mark kinds: rule, step, check, fact, card, goal and note.
More are added later and by the user. The card kind exists today
and moves to the marks folder. Extra fields of a mark, such as
level, every and minutes, live in their own block next to the mark
and not on the marked block.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
